    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_5d39173f447f4ff9a79972d7",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 20, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2335\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level, where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than 10, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units among those subjects that are degree-granting courses, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics courses (considering only departments that offer more than five courses), and the number of unique subject codes for Mathematics in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE table. List the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the number of unique subject codes, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3644\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a total of 1 unit, show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3163\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting and the total units are greater than 6, provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units offered, and the number of courses where the design units are at least 3. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3311\", \"desc\": \"For each course that has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', list the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, along with the department name, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses offered this year with non-null total units). Present the results ordered by course number and course number description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3078\", \"desc\": \"For each subject title and department name where the total units are greater than 3, give the number of offered sections, the minimum number of enrolled students, and the average lab units for those subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1766\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting, the total units are greater than 6, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, school name, number of distinct course options available, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students and departments whose name is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1023\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4683\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1049\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for its subjects in regular terms that are not the current term, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year (considering only departments that have more than five subjects offered in 2022, are degree-granting, and are not the Chemistry department)? Show the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for regular non-current terms, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_359\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the total number of lecture units for all subjects offered in regular terms by the Mathematics department (Course 18), where at least 60% of those subjects are undergraduate-level (HGN_DESC = 'Undergraduate'), considering only those academic years where the total lecture units are more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total lecture units across all academic years? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3867\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3989\", \"desc\": \"For each department and each subject offered in the academic year 2024, show the department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, term code, term description, and the highest minimum total units (in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by academic year) for that subject, along with the course description, subject code description, and the difference between the number of characters in the course description and the average number of characters in course descriptions for that department, for courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_39ca8f7a58f746f6811581ea",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"dw_1023\", \"name\": \"Math Fall Non-Variable Unit Statistics by Academic Year with Enrollment Filter\", \"category\": \"Subject Offering and Enrollment Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"sql\": \"WITH AcademicYearStats AS ( SELECT at.ACADEMIC_YEAR, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, VARIANCE(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS variance_total_units, STDDEV(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS stddev_total_units FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON ccso.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE WHERE ccso.IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM = 'Y' AND ccso.IS_VARIABLE_UNITS = 'N' AND ccso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY at.ACADEMIC_YEAR, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC ORDER BY at.ACADEMIC_YEAR ), DepartmentYearStats AS ( SELECT cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR, COUNT(DISTINCT ss.SUBJECT_ID) AS num_unique_subjects, MIN(ss.TOTAL_UNITS) AS min_total_units FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED cso JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON cso.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON at.TERM_CODE = ss.TERM_CODE AND cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME WHERE cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND ss.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER > 10 GROUP BY cso.DEPARTMENT_NAME, at.ACADEMIC_YEAR ) SELECT ays.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ays.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, dys.DEPARTMENT_NAME, dys.num_unique_subjects, dys.min_total_units, ays.variance_total_units, ays.stddev_total_units FROM AcademicYearStats ays JOIN DepartmentYearStats dys ON ays.ACADEMIC_YEAR = dys.ACADEMIC_YEAR WHERE dys.num_unique_subjects > 0 ORDER BY ays.ACADEMIC_YEAR;\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per academic year\"}, {\"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per department name per course level\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting, the total units are greater than 6, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, school name, number of distinct course options available, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students and departments whose name is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"id\": \"dw_1766\", \"name\": \"Math Degree-Granting Course Level Counts with Min Units, Course Options, and Highest Term Average Library Enrollment\", \"sql\": \"WITH highest_avg_enrollment AS ( WITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, l.TERM_CODE, AVG(l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment_per_term FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s JOIN LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED l ON s.COURSE_NUMBER = l.COURSE_NUMBER WHERE l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND s.DEPARTMENT_NAME IS NOT NULL AND s.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, l.TERM_CODE ) SELECT DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(avg_enrollment_per_term) AS highest_avg_enrollment_per_term FROM inner_cte GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME ), course_stats AS ( WITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT scd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, scd.COURSE_LEVEL, COUNT(DISTINCT scd.COURSE) AS course_count, MIN(ccc.TOTAL_UNITS) AS min_total_units FROM SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON scd.DEPARTMENT = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN CIS_COURSE_CATALOG ccc ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = ccc.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE scd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND ccc.TOTAL_UNITS > 6 AND scd.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '18' GROUP BY scd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, scd.COURSE_LEVEL ) SELECT icte.DEPARTMENT_NAME, icte.COURSE_LEVEL, icte.course_count, icte.min_total_units, scd.SCHOOL_NAME, COUNT(DISTINCT scd.COURSE_OPTION) AS distinct_course_options FROM inner_cte icte JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION scd ON icte.DEPARTMENT_NAME = scd.DEPARTMENT_NAME AND icte.COURSE_LEVEL = scd.COURSE_LEVEL GROUP BY icte.DEPARTMENT_NAME, icte.COURSE_LEVEL, icte.course_count, icte.min_total_units, scd.SCHOOL_NAME ) SELECT cs.DEPARTMENT_NAME, cs.COURSE_LEVEL, cs.course_count, cs.min_total_units, cs.SCHOOL_NAME, cs.distinct_course_options, hae.highest_avg_enrollment_per_term FROM course_stats cs JOIN highest_avg_enrollment hae ON cs.DEPARTMENT_NAME = hae.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY cs.DEPARTMENT_NAME, cs.COURSE_LEVEL;\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"name\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"CIS course catalog table: an alternative course catalog source with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags), keyed by academic year, term code, and subject identity. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via DEPARTMENT_CODE for subject code resolution.\", \"columns\": {\"IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether offered in the fall term\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_IAP\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether offered during IAP\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_SPRING_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether offered in the spring term\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_SUMMER_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether offered in the summer term\"}, \"FALL_INSTRUCTORS\": {\"desc\": \"Fall term instructor names\"}, \"SPRING_INSTRUCTORS\": {\"desc\": \"Spring term instructor names\"}, \"STATUS_CHANGE\": {\"desc\": \"Catalog status change indicator\"}, \"LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Date of last activity on the record\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier\"}, \"HASS_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"HASS attribute code\"}, \"HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"HASS attribute description\"}, \"TERM_DURATION\": {\"desc\": \"Duration within the term\"}, \"GLOBAL_REGIONS\": {\"desc\": \"Global regions associated with the subject\"}, \"GLOBAL_COUNTRIES\": {\"desc\": \"Global countries associated with the subject\"}, \"ON_LINE_PAGE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Online catalog page number\"}, \"ACADEMIC_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year of the catalog record\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER\"}, \"SUBJECT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject code, e.g. '18'\"}, \"SUBJECT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Subject number within the subject code\"}, \"SOURCE_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Source system subject identifier\"}, \"PRINT_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier as printed\"}, \"IS_PRINTED_IN_BULLETIN\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether printed in the bulletin\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Department code; joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE and SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name\"}, \"EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code from which catalog attributes take effect\"}, \"SUBJECT_SHORT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Short title of the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Full title of the subject; joins to CIS_COURSE_CATALOG-based subject title matching\"}, \"IS_VARIABLE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject has variable units\"}, \"LECTURE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Lecture credit units\"}, \"LAB_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Lab credit units\"}, \"PREPARATION_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Preparation credit units\"}, \"TOTAL_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Total credit units\"}, \"DESIGN_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Design credit units\"}, \"GRADE_TYPE\": {\"desc\": \"Grade type code\"}, \"GRADE_TYPE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Grade type description\"}, \"GRADE_RULE\": {\"desc\": \"Grade rule code\"}, \"GRADE_RULE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Grade rule description\"}, \"HGN_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"HGN level code\"}, \"HGN_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"HGN level description\"}, \"HGN_EXCEPT\": {\"desc\": \"HGN exception indicator\"}, \"GIR_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"General Institute Requirement attribute code\"}, \"GIR_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"General Institute Requirement attribute description\"}, \"COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Communication requirement attribute code\"}, \"COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Communication requirement attribute description\"}, \"TUITION_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Tuition attribute code\"}, \"TUITION_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Tuition attribute description\"}, \"WRITE_REQ_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Writing requirement attribute code\"}, \"WRITE_REQ_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Writing requirement attribute description\"}, \"SUPERVISOR_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Supervisor attribute code\"}, \"SUPERVISOR_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Supervisor attribute description\"}, \"PREREQUISITES\": {\"desc\": \"Prerequisite text\"}, \"SUBJECT_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Full catalog description text\"}, \"JOINT_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"Joint subjects list\"}, \"SCHOOL_WIDE_ELECTIVES\": {\"desc\": \"School-wide elective attribute\"}, \"MEETS_WITH_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"Subjects this one meets with\"}, \"EQUIVALENT_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"Equivalent subjects\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether offered this academic year\"}, \"IS_DESIGN_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for design section\"}, \"IS_LAB_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for lab section\"}, \"IS_LECTURE_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for lecture section\"}, \"IS_MASTER_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for master section\"}, \"IS_RECITATION_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for recitation section\"}, \"SECTION_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Section identifier\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code of the catalog record\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject per term in the CIS course catalog\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\", \"columns\": {\"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the subject offered summary record\"}, \"COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Composite subject key; joins to SUBJECT_OFFERED.COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Course number of the subject; joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER and SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, e.g. '18.01'; joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the subject identifier\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject title\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier for clustered subjects\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master subject identifier\"}, \"CLUSTER_TYPE\": {\"desc\": \"Cluster type code\"}, \"CLUSTER_TYPE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Cluster type description\"}, \"CLUSTER_LIST\": {\"desc\": \"List of subjects in the cluster\"}, \"HGN_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"HGN (Higgins) level code\"}, \"HGN_CODE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"HGN level description\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department code; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department name\"}, \"OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering school name, e.g. 'Engineering'; used for school-level filtering\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the faculty member responsible for the subject\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"MIT ID of the responsible faculty member\"}, \"TOTAL_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Total credit units of the subject\"}, \"LECTURE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Lecture credit units\"}, \"LAB_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Lab credit units\"}, \"PREPARATION_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Preparation credit units\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Enrollment number at the subject level\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Enrollment number of the cluster\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of students enrolled in the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_GROUPING_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Key to the subject grouping record\"}, \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Foreign key to SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject per term\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"name\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"desc\": \"Extended academic term dimension table covering all terms known to the warehouse (a superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS, including terms without full status tracking). Shares term calendar attributes (term code, dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, registration and class dates) but does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE or DROP_DATE columns.\", \"columns\": {\"ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the academic term record; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format, e.g. '2019FA'\"}, \"TERM_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Human-readable term description\"}, \"TERM_SELECTOR\": {\"desc\": \"Term selector label used for picklists\"}, \"TERM_START_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Term start date\"}, \"TERM_END_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Term end date\"}, \"ACADEMIC_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year the term belongs to\"}, \"ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year description text\"}, \"IS_CURRENT_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag indicating whether the term is the current term\"}, \"TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR\": {\"desc\": \"Single-character term status indicator: 'P'=Previous, 'C'=Current, 'F'=Future, 'None'=Unspecified\"}, \"FINANCIAL_AID_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Financial aid year the term maps to; used to partition running sums by financial aid year\"}, \"DEGREE_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Degree year the term maps to\"}, \"LAST_DAY_OF_FINAL_EXAM\": {\"desc\": \"Last day of final exams for the term\"}, \"PRE_REGISTRATION_START_DAY\": {\"desc\": \"First day of pre-registration for the term\"}, \"REGISTRATION_DAY\": {\"desc\": \"Registration day for the term\"}, \"FIRST_DAY_OF_CLASSES\": {\"desc\": \"First day of classes in the term\"}, \"LAST_DAY_OF_CLASSES\": {\"desc\": \"Last day of classes in the term\"}, \"GRADUATE_AWARD_START_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Start date of the graduate award period\"}, \"GRADUATE_AWARD_END_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"End date of the graduate award period\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date of the record\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per academic term (all terms)\"}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
