    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_00bc719de3004999b71d3e2c",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 15, \"items_by_type\": {\"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1049\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for its subjects in regular terms that are not the current term, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year (considering only departments that have more than five subjects offered in 2022, are degree-granting, and are not the Chemistry department)? Show the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for regular non-current terms, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3163\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting and the total units are greater than 6, provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units offered, and the number of courses where the design units are at least 3. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2335\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level, where the total number of enrolled students in offered subjects is greater than 10, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units among those subjects that are degree-granting courses, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for Mathematics courses (considering only departments that offer more than five courses), and the number of unique subject codes for Mathematics in the SIS_SUBJECT_CODE table. List the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the number of unique subject codes, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2924\", \"desc\": \"For degree-granting courses in the School of Engineering, show the course description, department name, subject title, and the subject's grade type description, but only include those courses where the total units for the subject exceed the average total units for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_359\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the total number of lecture units for all subjects offered in regular terms by the Mathematics department (Course 18), where at least 60% of those subjects are undergraduate-level (HGN_DESC = 'Undergraduate'), considering only those academic years where the total lecture units are more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total lecture units across all academic years? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3644\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a total of 1 unit, show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1766\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting, the total units are greater than 6, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, school name, number of distinct course options available, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students and departments whose name is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_41\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, provide the academic year description and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered in terms that are not the current term, have a term status indicator of 'P', are offered by the Mathematics department, and are full term subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4387\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering with total student enrollment in its courses greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and with total enrollment greater than 50), display the department name, the total number of students enrolled in its courses, and the highest average total units for subjects it has ever offered in a regular academic term, listing the results in descending order of total enrollment. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_40e347a46be44e7b897ec29b",
      "name": "semantic_graph",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 12, \"items\": [{\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"SIS subject code lookup table mapping subject codes and course numbers to their descriptions, departments, and schools. Used to resolve subject code descriptions and to link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\", \"name\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"name\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"SIS subject code lookup table mapping subject codes and course numbers to their descriptions, departments, and schools. Used to resolve subject code descriptions and to link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\", \"name\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) lookup table: one row per six-digit CIP program code, classifying instructional programs into a two-digit category and a four-digit series, with program/category/four-digit titles, a change note, the CIP revision version year (1990/2000/2010/2020), and the warehouse load date. Joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs, categories, and schools/departments; CIP_WITH_VERSION is the multi-version variant keeping every revision of each program code.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"CIP\", \"name\": \"CIP\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Versioned Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) lookup table: one row per CIP program code per revision version year (1990/2000/2010/2020), preserving the historical classification of each program across CIP revisions. Carries the same program/category/four-digit code and title attributes as CIP plus a surrogate key, but no NOTE column and fewer distinct program codes than CIP. Joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE (matching more course rows than CIP because a program code can appear under several versions); use CIP when one row per program code is required.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"CIP_WITH_VERSION\", \"name\": \"CIP_WITH_VERSION\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"CIS course catalog table: an alternative course catalog source with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags), keyed by academic year, term code, and subject identity. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via DEPARTMENT_CODE for subject code resolution.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"name\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"outgoing\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"name\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"joins\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\", \"entity_type\": \"table\", \"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"name\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\"}, {\"relation_type\": \"column_concept\", \"direction\": \"incoming\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\", \"entity_type\": \"column_concept\", \"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"name\": \"Department Name\"}]}"
    },
