e summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1335\", \"desc\": \"List, for each department, either (a) the department's full name, the range and variance of the total units for degree-granting Mathematics department courses offered in the 2008 academic year along with the long course description for each course (with the reason 'Math 2008 Stats'), or (b) the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units) where the average total units is greater than the overall average across all departments (with the reason 'High Avg Units'). Show the columns in the following order: department name, total units range, total units variance, average total units, standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, long course description, and reason for inclusion. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4061\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4701\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the academic year, academic year description, the geometric mean of the number of library reserve material details per subject offered (considering only records where the material status is 'U' and the academic term is a regular term), the average total units, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units, and the average number of design units for subjects that are offered in the fall term and have a material status of 'U' in the library reserve? List the results ordered by the geometric mean of materials per subject in descending order, then by the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1023\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_359\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the total number of lecture units for all subjects offered in regular terms by the Mathematics department (Course 18), where at least 60% of those subjects are undergraduate-level (HGN_DESC = 'Undergraduate'), considering only those academic years where the total lecture units are more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total lecture units across all academic years? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1301\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, where the maximum number of total units for any Mathematics (Course 18) subject offered in that year is greater than 9 and there are more than 5 Mathematics subjects offered in the fall term, what are the academic year, the maximum total units, the corresponding term description, the subject title, the academic year description, the standard deviation (us