061, dw_2597 | none found for regular-term stats | dw_1049 (Math only, regular non-current terms) |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- \"course level\", \"course is degree granting\", \"design units ≥ 3 course count\" → only SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION (COURSE_LEVEL, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING) + CIS_COURSE_CATALOG (DESIGN_UNITS, TOTAL_UNITS) SUPPORTED — exactly the dw_3163 precedent; SUBJECT_SUMMARY/CCSO lack COURSE_LEVEL → NOT-SUPPORTED.\n- \"academic year description\" → ACADEMIC_TERMS.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC SUPPORTED; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL also has it but lacks IS_REGULAR_TERM → VIOLATES the \"regular terms\" filter.\n- \"regular terms\" → ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y' SUPPORTED.\n- \"average and STDDEV of total units … in that department and year\" + \"deviation of each subject's total units\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED per dw_3417/dw_4061 precedent SUPPORTED.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"department name\" maps to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME (Part 1, per dw_3163) and COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME (Part 2, per dw_4061); column_concept_department_name confirms both share the same academic value domain, so joining the two parts on DEPARTMENT_NAME is valid. \"subjects offered in regular terms\" anchors to ACADEMIC_TERMS.IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y' (only in ACADEMIC_TERMS). \"academic year description\" anchors to ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** Part-1 shape precedents: 3 (dw_3163, dw_1766, dw_2335) — all on SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION + SIS_DEPARTMENT + CIS_COURSE_CATALOG. Regular-term TOTAL_UNITS avg/STDDEV precedents: 2 (dw_3417, dw_4061) — both on ACADEMIC_TERMS ⋈ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED via EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE. Deviation precedents: dw_2597, dw_104, dw_1758 (value − group average).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\ndw_3163-family metrics answer course-catalog/department accreditation-style questions; dw_3417/dw_4061-family answer yearly unit-dispersion questions per department using the catalog's effective-term linkage; the two families are joined in composite questions via the shared DEPARTMENT_NAME domain.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase-1 entities investigated: tables SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, SIS_DEPARTMENT (semantic_get); metrics dw_3163, dw_3417, dw_2597, dw_1049, dw_1023, dw_1766, dw_41, dw_104, dw_4061 (semantic_get full SQL); concepts/column-concepts reviewed via search descriptions; graph traversals on SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION and CIS_COURSE_CATALOG. Remaining search hits (facilities/HR/IAP/library/TIP entities) are unrelated to the task and were discarded per screening rules. **Note: `mysql_query` is unavailable in this session (persistent \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\"), so data verification could not be performed; the SQL follows verified precedent metric SQL exactly.**\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n**6a.** Part 1: dw_3163's exact SQL (SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ⋈ SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ CIS_COURSE_CATALOG; IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'; TOTAL_UNITS>6; two-level aggregation for course_count, min_total_units, design-units≥3 course count). Part 2: dw_3417/dw_4061 pattern (ACADEMIC_TERMS ⋈ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON TERM_CODE=EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE, IS_REGULAR_TERM='Y'), grouped by DEPARTMENT_NAME+ACADEMIC_YEAR for AVG/STDDEV, with per-subject rows and deviation = TOTAL_UNITS − dept-year average. Join both parts on DEPARTMENT_NAME.\n\n**6b/6c.** Two-level aggregation avoids fan-out corruption; bare `STDDEV()` per instructions; no rounding; SELECT list has exactly the 12 requested columns in order. Data perspective: all required columns verified to exist via retrieved column definitions. Semantic-network perspective: every join path and filter is copied from retrieved precedent metric SQL (dw_3163, dw_3417, dw_4061, dw_2597). Business perspective: the question is a verbatim composition of dw_3163's text plus the regular-term subject-stats